---
import { ROBUSTNESS_DIMENSIONS } from '../../data/metrics';
---

<section class="section" id="robustness" aria-labelledby="robustness-h">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--split">
      <div>
        <p class="section-num">12 · Robustness</p>
        <h2 id="robustness-h">Does the winner survive different assumptions?</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-sub" data-reveal>
        A model that wins under one assumption may not win under another. Testing the range is part of the research question, not a footnote to it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="sens" data-reveal>
      {ROBUSTNESS_DIMENSIONS.map((d) => (
        <div class="sens__row">
          <div class="sens__meta">
            <p class="mono sens__label">{d.label}</p>
            <p class="sens__note">{d.note}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sens__scale" role="img" aria-label={`${d.label}: low to medium to high`}>
            <span class="sens__tick sens__tick--lo" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="sens__tick sens__tick--mid" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="sens__tick sens__tick--hi" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="mono sens__range">{d.range}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="sens-note" data-reveal>
      <span class="mono sens-note__label">Why this matters</span>
      If the best approach changes under reasonable alternatives, that is an important finding — not a problem with the experiment. Findings are reported with the assumptions they depend on.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .sens {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-1);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .sens__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: var(--sp-6);
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--sp-5) var(--sp-6);
  }
  .sens__row + .sens__row { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  @media (max-width: 44rem) {
    .sens__row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--sp-3); }
  }
  .sens__label { font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--sp-1); }
  .sens__note { color: var(--ink-3); font-size: var(--fs-body-sm); }

  .sens__scale {
    position: relative;
    width: min(22rem, 60vw);
    height: 3.6rem;
  }
  .sens__scale::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.5rem; right: 0.5rem;
    top: 50%;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--line-2);
  }
  .sens__tick {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .sens__tick--lo { left: 0.5rem; height: 0.7rem; }
  .sens__tick--mid { left: 50%; height: 1rem; }
  .sens__tick--hi { right: 0.5rem; height: 0.7rem; }
  .sens__range {
    position: absolute;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0.1rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: var(--fs-mono-sm);
  }

  .sens-note {
    margin-top: var(--sp-6);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
  }
  .sens-note__label { display: block; color: var(--c-uncertainty); margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); }
</style>